  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Alcazar Energy Partners II SCSP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main project-level effect is on stakeholders through the increased affordability of renewable energy capacity in the target markets as well as the associated environmental effects through decarbonizing power generation and displacing aging baseload. Beyond the project, the investment is expected to help enhance the power sector resilience through diversifying the energy mix in the target markets.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed project involves up to US$40 million of equity in Alcazar Energy Partners II (&apos;AEP II&apos;),  a closed end infrastructure fund with a target size of US$500m. AEP II will invest in a diversified portfolio of renewable energy (&apos;RE&apos;) projects across selected emerging markets with a primary focus on onshore wind, solar PV and storage in MENA, Eastern Europe and Central Asia.</narrative>
  </description>
